WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.960
Speaker 1: All right, so now let's get to
that story that I alluded to earlier.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.940
Dozens of you emailing me and saying, David,
what is happening?

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:15.880
Tulsi Gabbard is speaking at C-PAC, the Conservative
Political Action Conference.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:17.690
What the hell is going on here?

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:18.830
Let's discuss it.

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:23.289
This weekend actually started starting Thursday
night and our coverage will start Thursday

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:24.539
as well.

00:00:24.539 --> 00:00:27.730
CPAC is happening in Florida.

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:33.820
CPAC, the Conservative Political Action Conference,
is a sort of who's who of Republicans, right

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:38.750
wing extremists, religious conservatives,
conspiracy theorists and all of these other

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:42.820
different aspects of the American right wing.

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:49.800
And as a guest, they are having former Democratic
congresswoman, former Democratic presidential

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:54.010
candidate Tulsi Gabbard, who I thought was
on the left.

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:59.540
And in fact, while she was running in the
Democratic primary, you had people who said

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:03.100
this is the only true liberal left.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:08.640
This is the only true leftist left because
people fell for it, she would say regime change

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:14.829
wars and endless wars, and people would say,
Oh, she's so great, she's so fantastic.

00:01:14.829 --> 00:01:21.810
Notice that CPAC promotion of Tulsi doesn't
even mention that she was a Democratic presidential

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:22.810
candidate.

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:25.159
It doesn't say that she was a Democratic congresswoman.

00:01:25.159 --> 00:01:30.600
It just says presidential candidate and people
fell for this stuff.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:34.579
I didn't, and you all know that, and some
of you did.

00:01:34.579 --> 00:01:38.600
And I told you day after day, you're being
tricked.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:41.100
Don't fall for it, don't fall for it.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:48.420
The buzzwords she would use would make leftists
some leftists fawn all over her.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:52.770
She's against wars and stuff, so she's good.

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:58.469
And I'd criticize her and I'd be called the
DNC tool and a DNC plant.

00:01:58.469 --> 00:02:03.740
And part of the concerted effort to take away
attention from Tulsi or whatever.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:05.359
In fact, I did quite the opposite.

00:02:05.359 --> 00:02:06.880
Even by just talking about her.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:10.830
Most of my audience was like, David, she's
completely irrelevant to this race.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.489
Why are you even talking about her?

00:02:12.489 --> 00:02:17.129
And it was because, you know, people were
telling me some people were saying, David,

00:02:17.129 --> 00:02:19.860
she's the only real liberal.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:23.580
She has a much better shot of winning the
Republican nomination than the Democratic

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:24.840
nomination.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:30.280
And I am issuing a call right now to the people
who got bamboozled by her.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:33.519
Just stand up and say, I got tricked.

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:35.299
I'm going to do better next time.

00:02:35.299 --> 00:02:36.599
It's OK.

00:02:36.599 --> 00:02:37.599
Just admit it.

00:02:37.599 --> 00:02:39.650
It happens to all of us.

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:43.740
But I also want to include something serious
on this.

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:47.459
It's not just about we were obviously right
about to see.

00:02:47.459 --> 00:02:49.070
It's not OK.

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:54.210
There's a very good tweet that our friend
Farron Cousins from Ring of Fire put out about

00:02:54.210 --> 00:03:00.459
CPAC and he said, quote, We're all going to
spend the next week mocking C-PAC while ignoring

00:03:00.459 --> 00:03:05.950
the fact that we don't have the level of organization
or attention.

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:09.379
We don't have that level of organization or
attention on the left.

00:03:09.379 --> 00:03:12.120
We're at a tremendous disadvantage.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.300
And that rarely gets mentioned.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:17.590
And Farron is exactly right.

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:19.890
I've been screaming for a decade.

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:21.510
They are better than us at this.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.079
They are better than us.

00:03:23.079 --> 00:03:29.450
The left barely even funds independent media,
never mind something like CPAC.

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:34.510
The right understands you've got to pour money
into on campus stuff.

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:36.250
You've got to pour money into.

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:39.510
Young professionals and getting them over
to your way of thinking.

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:40.959
You've got to have events.

00:03:40.959 --> 00:03:44.750
You've got to have people who feel like they're
part of something.

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:45.980
You've got to fund media.

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:50.219
They fund Turning Point USA and all sorts
of different right wing shows.

00:03:50.219 --> 00:03:54.920
We have almost none of it on the left, and
they love to say, Oh, but George Soros is

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:59.299
pouring money into this, that the other thing,
et cetera, et cetera.

00:03:59.299 --> 00:04:04.129
The left barely funds this type of stuff in
the right way.

00:04:04.129 --> 00:04:10.129
And when I talk about, hey, you know, like
only half of one percent of our audience is

00:04:10.129 --> 00:04:12.390
our members on our website.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:16.090
I'm not just saying, Hey, it'd be cool if
you supported our work.

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:23.289
I'm also saying at a certain point, we've
got to fund the things that we think are important

00:04:23.289 --> 00:04:31.009
and having a big infrastructure of right wing
media and right wing activism all coming together

00:04:31.009 --> 00:04:33.360
is a really big deal for the right.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:34.520
It just is.

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:36.440
There's no way around it.

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:42.150
There's this conference Netroots Nation I
used to go to on the left, and I think it's

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:44.080
like the biggest thing the left has.

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:45.530
And it's it's not great.

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:47.130
You know, I have friends who still work over
there.

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:48.130
It's not great.

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:53.640
First of all, you know how I often say to
you guys, these little toxic elements of the

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:59.580
left are very, very small, like the the right
loves to say, Oh, the left is all identity

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:02.289
politics and woke stirrers and all this different
stuff.

00:05:02.289 --> 00:05:06.300
And I explain to you, it's actually really
small netroots, which was like the only thing

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:11.289
we had unfortunately overrepresented some
of those toxic elements of the left.

00:05:11.289 --> 00:05:13.030
I don't even know if Netroots still exists.

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:18.060
I know they did some online only stuff, but
like if that's the best we have and the right

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:24.639
has CPAC turning point USA, all of these different
think tanks, and they're so well-funded, how

00:05:24.639 --> 00:05:26.130
can we hope to compete?

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:29.919
So yes, we are going to ridicule the things
said at CPAC.

00:05:29.919 --> 00:05:34.640
I will be live with CPAC coverage Thursday,
Friday, Saturday, Sunday.

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:36.880
It's going to be a huge weekend of insanity.

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:37.880
We're going to laugh at it.

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:39.550
It's going to be funny to some degree.

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:42.639
But in the back of it, we have to remember
they are so much better organized than we

00:05:42.639 --> 00:05:43.810
are.

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:49.300
And unless we can get it together, even though
the country keeps moving to the left, the

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:50.790
electorate keeps moving to the left.

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:54.960
If you look at issues, they're going to keep
winning, they're going to keep winning and

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:56.310
we need to understand that

